    "description": "CenTrio provides district heating, cooling, and electricity services through urban energy systems in major U.S. cities. Its customers or end markets include universities, hospitals, school districts, commercial buildings, and other large real estate users. The operating model is an asset-heavy utility model based on long-lived central plants and networked thermal systems. Operations are concentrated in nine U.S. cities including Chicago, Houston, New Orleans, Denver, Seattle, Portland, Los Angeles, Syracuse, and San Francisco-area locations. Public materials indicate service to more than 370 customers across roughly 170 million square feet according to QIC. Current ownership reflects QIC and Ullico’s completion of the CenTrio acquisition in 2021, with QIC disclosing a 75% interest.",
